                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "TLDR: Amazing sound track, but too short, too easy, and too disrespectful to your time. \n\n[b][u]General Thoughts/Overview:[/u][/b]\n\nThe Low Road (LR) is a point and click adventure with a spy theme. \nWe are Noomi Kovacs, liar, manipulator, cheat, pickpocket, and recently minted espionage graduate. We’re also getting our first job, and can’t be dealing with a slow burn career. And so begins our race to the field, as we levy our craft against the very people employing us in a cartoonish plot of deceit and villainy.\n\n[b][u]Pros:[/u][/b]\n[list][*] The music absolutely slaps. The voice acting isn’t too shabby either. \n[*] The choices you make do have some material impact in the game, dialogue is remembered and actions have consequences. Even though this is brief, that’s a nice touch. \n[*] The overarching story is actually pretty decent, even if it’s whacky, despite the not great moment to moment writing. \n[/list]\n\n[b][u]Cons:[/u][/b]\n[list][*] It’s painfully short and highly limited in scope. This feels like another demo no one could be arsed to flesh out and then thrown on the market with a full price. \n[*] It’s so painfully simple, and relies a lot on ‘gotcha’ a lot to extend the puzzles an extra step. This is rather frustrating. \n[*] The character moves so slowly, and animations going up and down stairs take so long, that I can only assume it was done to stop you completing inside the refund window, going “that’s it?!” and calling it in. \n[/list]\n\n[b][u]Suggested improvements:[/u][/b]\n[list][*] A skip animation button. \n[*] A double-click to run.\n[*] A full length game. \n[/list]\n\n[b][u]Overall Recommendation:[/u][/b]\n\nI think this has to be a no. Why? Because even though it’s less than three hours long, I can’t bring myself to 100% it. I just don’t want to play it again at all. I can’t think of anything more damning than that. \n\nThis is a game for people who want something short and easy, this is a game for someone who wants an absolutely banging 70’s inspired track that makes it feel like an epic spy adventure, and this is a game for someone who wants to have a limited choices matter adventure. I also heartily recommend this to people new to point and click adventures, or with very limited patience for adventure games. \n\nThis is not a game for a point and click veteran looking for a challenge, it is not for people looking for a full and detailed game, and it isn’t for someone after an actual, serious, and intrigue based spy thriller. \n\nI thought I was going to love this when I started, the music hit me hard and the game started really well… it’s a shame it just never really delivered.  \n\n[url=https://store.steampowered.com/curator/44852412/]My curator page[/url] with reviews by genre. In case you want to find more games, or even reviews, like this one.",
